WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.330
This is the Microsoft for Education Daily, for Wednesday.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.920
Here's what shipped at Microsoft in the last 24 hours.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.600
Stay current. Ohio State and Microsoft announced a five-year partnership for care,

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:22.240
research and education.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:26.490
Expect more AI learning and Microsoft certifications for students,

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:28.000
staff and the community.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:37.200
For student coders, .NET 11 is out, with C# 15 and two years of support.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:42.650
New union types make the compiler check every case,

00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:44.890
and .NET Conf runs through Friday.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:49.050
Coding in Visual Studio 2026?

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:53.030
Copilot Chat just got a new engine, built by GitHub.

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:59.480
In Microsoft's own test, it solved 21 more coding tasks with the same model.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.200
Git on your lab computers? Update it: the new release fixes six security flaws.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:11.960
The worst lets a malicious repo run code when it's cloned with its submodules.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.630
Refreshing student laptops?

00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:21.770
Windows settings backup and restore moves their settings and app list to the new PC.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:25.630
A new restore summary shows what came back,

00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:28.470
and from 26H2, backup's on by default.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.380
Something calmer for computer science classes: Microsoft

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:36.870
researchers found memory bugs in Rust's standard library.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:40.320
An AI scanner helped them show that even safe

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:43.270
Rust can trip over the unsafe code underneath.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:50.640
The fine print? Power BI's R and Python visuals retire in May 2027.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:54.980
Idle course repos? From December 8,

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:59.670
GitHub pauses their Dependabot alerts; one push brings them back.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:02.700
After hours,

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:08.030
Minecraft launched Realms Pro: private servers for up to 50 players at once.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:14.210
That's five times Realms Plus, on its own server with 16 GB of RAM.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:20.540
And big build crews can edit together, live, in Minecraft Editor on Windows.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:27.920
Learn something new, update Git, check your old repos and reports: stay current.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.020
Day after day, the updates keep stacking up.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.690
On the release board: shipped, and still shipping.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.410
That was 24 hours at Microsoft. Tomorrow, there's more.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.720
This has been the Microsoft for Education Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.310
Stay curious. See you tomorrow.
